Sting is a very nice option here because it allows you to split out the 
foocubi and Kops and deal with them one by one without being very high 
level to start with.  It sets up a seamless and painless jump from level 
3 protection racket to level 30+ and all suited up.  (Plus you get a 
combat bonus when attacking somebody who's stuck in a web if you don't 
have a ranged attack handy.)

Chaotic human is the key for a low-level altar conversion.

Playing as a wizard lets you start with MR (so you own any polytrap) and 
can use the same polytrap twice, once for your pet for gold (and to 
depriest afterwards) and a second time to web the level.

Finally a wizard has the best chance of being able to ID the rings you 
get from Sokoban.

My best guess is that with moderately careful play this trick will work 
one time in four as written.  (The odds of having the ring of Polymorph 
Control at that point in time.)

The only safer place to farm is on the Wizard's Quest final level.

